This application's look follows MyMonero's web wallet
(https://github.com/mymonero/mymonero-web-js, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c)
2014-2019, MyMonero.com), read at the default branch on 2026-09-14, together
with its desktop sibling (https://github.com/mymonero/mymonero-app-js, same
licence and copyright).

Files carrying that work
------------------------

  src/styles/tokens.css   the surface and text ramps, the elevation recipe,
                          the type scale and the tracking, the radii, the
                          control heights
  src/styles/app.css      the component recipes those tokens build: the sunken
                          input, the uppercase field label, the balance at 32 px
                          with its fraction dimmed, the two-part elevation
  src/components/UI/      the shapes those recipes are used in: the three
                          button colours and their geometry, the panel, the
                          label-over-value field row, the notice box
  src/components/TabBar.tsx
                          the four-destination tab bar along the bottom

What is carried over is the design system those stylesheets state by
repetition, and the screen flow: a landing that offers "Create new wallet" and
"Use existing wallet", a wallet screen whose balance is the largest thing on
it with the transaction list under it, a send screen with the fee on its own
line and a named sending state, a receive screen that is an address and its QR
code, and a settings screen that holds the lock and the server address. The
copy keeps that wallet's register: short sentences, sentence case in prose,
uppercase field labels.

No file was copied. Where a value is MyMonero's it is stated as a custom
property in `tokens.css`, which the original does not have, and the components
are written against those properties rather than against inline styles.

What is not carried over: the accent colour, which is the one value in that
palette carrying MyMonero's identity, replaced by Qnero's own; the yellow
notice fill that goes with it, because that yellow is eleven degrees of hue
from Qnero's amber where it is a hundred and forty-one from MyMonero's cyan,
so the notice here is a border and the secondary ink; the light palette, which
is this project's; and the `Native-*` typefaces, which are a licensed retail
family outside the BSD grant on the source, whose roles are filled by system
stacks instead.

BSD-3-Clause clause 3 forbids using the copyright holder's or contributors'
names to endorse or promote products derived from this software. The MyMonero
name and logo appear nowhere in this application. The credit is in
`README.md`, as a statement of provenance.

